# Python cache and compiled files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Raw/private data; keep the expected directory structure locally.
# ``after_split_data/`` and ``reference_code/`` were archived into ``bin/`` on
# 2026-09-21; these rules carry no leading slash, so they keep matching at any
# depth and ``bin/after_split_data/`` / ``bin/reference_code/`` stay ignored too.
raw_data/
after_split_data/
reference_code/

# Relabelled datasets built by ``raw_data/relabel_by_thickness.py`` (one folder
# per threshold scheme, ~96 MB each). Derived data, same policy as ``raw_data/``
# -- regenerate with the script instead of committing it. Note that
# ``raw_data/`` above also hides the script itself; it is tracked via
# ``git add -f raw_data/relabel_by_thickness.py``.
raw_data_relabeled/

# Reproducible generated experiment and visualization outputs.
# Use ``experiments/*`` rather than ``experiments/``: the directory itself stays
# visible to git so the ``!`` rule below can keep its notes tracked.
experiments/*
!experiments/*.md
visualizations/

# Local archives and scratch run directories.
# ``bin/`` is the project attic (2026-09-21): one-off / unused scripts plus the
# archived snapshot folders (``bin/backup``, ``bin/_smoke_all``, ...). The rules
# below only match *directories*, so the files sitting directly in ``bin/``
# (``bin/_recon.ps1``, ``bin/visualize_dyn_envelope_cases.py``) stay tracked.
# They also match at any depth, so ``bin/backup/`` and the ``bin/_*/`` copies
# remain ignored as well.
backup/
smoke_test/
smoke_all/
_*/
